From b5cd2fa42aeeac2f6c91e01732d87b972c20991b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:27:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the missing off switches: close board, Start on /teacher,
 exit-ticket drafts

Site-code only. No Notion lesson content, states or structure touched.

Work space could be opened but never closed
- The iPad Remote rendered only "Open work space". hide-board was wired end to
  end - action type, control-remote handler, /control listener - and nothing in
  any UI ever sent it, so once the writing surface was up it covered the slide
  for the rest of the lesson. The deck key is now a toggle driven by
  presentation.boardOpen.

Start was buried in /control
- /teacher's live-session card gets a Start lesson button posting start-lesson
  to /api/control-remote. That is the complete server-side start - it seeds the
  sequence, flips broadcast to Live Class Flow and arms step zero - so no
  /control tab has to be open. The old path through /control?run=1 hard-blocks
  when no session is open and reports it only in a status line.

Exit ticket answers could vanish
- Drafts now back to localStorage per ticket id, restored when the ticket
  reopens and cleared on submit. Answers lived in React state alone, so a
  discarded tab lost a half-written exit ticket with no trace. That was the one
  real data-loss path in the student flow, and it matters more now that the
  exit ticket carries the hook problem rather than a procedure question.

A multiple-choice step with no authored choices rendered an empty box
- Indistinguishable from a frozen screen, with no way for a student to tell the
  difference or report it. It now says so.

